Package: lidarscan
Version: @VERSION@
Section: science
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Maintainer: LidarScan <support@lidarscan.invalid>
Homepage: https://lidarscan.invalid
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.35),
 libstdc++6 (>= 12),
 libqt6core6 (>= 6.4),
 libqt6gui6 (>= 6.4),
 libqt6widgets6 (>= 6.4),
 libqt6network6 (>= 6.4),
 libqt6serialport6 (>= 6.4),
 libvulkan1,
 libx11-6,
 libxcb1
Recommends: mesa-vulkan-drivers
Description: Lidar capture, review and floor-plan workstation
 LidarScan captures point clouds from a COIN-D6 (USB serial) or a Livox
 Mid-360 (Ethernet), reviews them in a GPU point-cloud viewer, measures
 distances, extracts 2D floor plans, merges multiple sessions and exports
 PLY / LAS / PCD / DXF / PDF.
 .
 This package installs a udev rule so the COIN-D6's CH340 USB-serial
 interface is usable without adding yourself to the dialout group, and
 registers the .lscan / .lscan.zip file types with the desktop.
 .
 The 3D viewport currently requires X11; on a Wayland session the bundled
 desktop entry starts the application under XWayland automatically.
